wooledge@skybridge.SCL.CWRU.Edu (Gregory Wooledge) writes:

>Klaus.Moeller@arbi.informatik.uni-oldenburg.de (Klaus Moeller) writes:

>>The first thing to wish for (only if you don't have it already, of course):
>>a very good weapon,

>Boots of speed are better.  If a monster can't hit you, it doesn't matter how
>long it takes you to chip away at him.  Then, you can always get an artifact
>from an altar, or even a fountain.

From my experience :
Most monsters that can hit you even at AC0, hit you hard, espeacilly on
the deeper levels. To get rid of them, you have to hit them harder.
Most players get the very high hit points very late in the game.
When they meet a nurse or gain lot of exp. levels and high constitution.

>>Second: Wish for good armor. Gray dragon scale mail +2 works well, if you have
>>it or are AC -5 or better and have something like shield of reflection,
>>cloak of magic resistance or a wand of polymorph, wish for gauntlets of
>>dexterity +2. Your Chance to hit depends on dexterity, not on strength.
>>(Strength accounts for damage).

>DON'T forget the speed boots!  That's "blessed +3 pair of speed boots".

I would never wish for speed boots, most classes have the intrinsic 'fast'
Archeologist, Elves and Samurais are fast from the beginning, Barbarians,
Caveman, Knights and Valkyries get fast at the 7th level. Easy to get
to this level for these classes for an experienced player.
The other classes get fast when eating a Quantum mechanic.
Eat them only once, if you're fast and eat one, your speed gets back to
normal.

>If it's early in the game, though, the gray dragon scale mail is VERY nice.
>But, later on, just get the wand of polymorph and make the armor yourself.

Right.

>>Don't wish for rings of teleport control, you get this intrinsic by eating
>>tengus and nymphs.

>Tengus, yes.  Nymphs, NO.
Tengus for teleportcontrol and teleport, nymphs and leprechauns only for
teleport

>>One word to armor : My favorite Armoring are
>>Blessed Hawaiian shirt (enchanted later)
>>Blesed gary dragon scale mail (magic resistance)
>>Shield of reflection
>>Gauntlets of dexterity (enchanted to a least +5)
>>boots of water walking (not levitaion, you can't pick things up)
>>Leather Hat or (if rust proof) Helm of brilliance
>>Cloak of displacement (works best when invisible)

>I'll take a Helm of Telepathy over brilliance.  But, then, I'm more of the
>hack-and-slash type of player.  I can't think of any reason to get the leather
>hat.  Just rust-proof your helmet.

I prefer the high intelligence gained by helms of brilliance, that allows
yoiu all the spells like remove curse, etc.
Spells are often better than scrolls, because they have no weight, and
can be used more than once. Rem curse is especially useful when fighting
with monsters that curse your items, scrolls of rem curse might become
cursed themselves. I use the leather hat only when my helmet is not
rust proof, the leather helmet is.

>Get speed boots and a ring of levitation.  The ring can be put on to allow
>water walking (and #dipping), while still giving you the double-speed.

What I've said before about levitation, you can't pick things up when
levitating. Water walking is better because it allows you to be
uncautious about pools.
Besides, speed boots aren't rust proof, can be anoying.

>Other indispensable NetHack items are: a lizard corpse, a lock pick (or the
>equivalent), a blindfold, and a unicorn horn.

Lock pick: best is a skeleton key, every shopkeeper has one.
Unicorn horn: Sorry I forgot this one, very important when fighting with
	      Jubilex or Demogorgon, kill a unicorn of opposite alignment.
Blind fold: Used for Medusa, but work better than a helm of telepathy
	    when eating a floating eye. Shows you the whole level.


